From 849bb719f86e317ca6a729e0cd71590af770c21c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 23:57:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06841/11362] ARC round-2 (codex): lf52 L3 -> L4 (+1), L5
 progress, on relaunch

Continuation of the same-day breadth-campaign game loop, on a relaunch
(45-minute budget) after the first attempt hit the 1800s process timeout.
The previously-documented "L4 partially cracked" three-peg deadlock is a
two-carrier relay: lower the peg-loaded vertical carrier until a
surviving torch is adjacent, align the empty horizontal carrier as a
landing socket, hop the peg through the indestructible torch, then
shuttle it between torch columns to merge the isolated pegs.

Self-run reproduction gate passed cleanly; independently re-verified by
the outer loop: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via the fixed resolver, all
5 confirmed reached_level=4. L5 introduces a genuinely movable torch (a
carrier can transport it through rail junctions); merged the two initial
pegs and reached a larger four-peg hub, but two mapping attempts both
stranded all four pegs via local merges. No L5 win this session.

reproducible_total_levels: 137 -> 138 (verified against a fresh sum). All
18 round-2 games now processed (17 with an artifact; 1 still awaiting
s5i5's relaunch).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
